    "narrative": "With the July 16th slate presenting a condensed window for the Austin Waves, our offensive focus is narrowed significantly by several key team off-days. Despite the limited pool, **Heliot Ramos** and **Jackson Merrill** emerge as the foundational pillars for today\u2019s scoring, both benefiting from favorable park factors that push their daily efficiency scores well into the \"Strong\" category. While **Jorge Polanco** currently holds a marginal score of 52.33, he remains our primary pivot point against Aaron Nola. The decision to keep **Jorge Polanco** in the lineup despite the 3.87 xERA of the opposing pitcher is driven by his reliable spot in the order, though we are monitoring a 31% rain risk in Philadelphia that could force a mid-game swap if the game enters a prolonged delay.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves the final infield slot, where **Brayan Rocchio** was narrowly edged out by the superior sprint speed profile of **Nasim Nunez**. In a league where stolen base scarcity dictates our value floor, the optimizer prioritized **Nasim Nunez** for his late-inning pinch-running upside and defensive security, despite **Brayan Rocchio** offering a marginally higher raw contact rate. We are currently navigating a depleted bench; with **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** all idle due to team off-days, and **Luis Robert Jr.** remaining sidelined on the IL, our offensive ceiling is heavily reliant on the high-contact approach of **Andy Pages** and **Jordan Westburg** to stabilize our AVG and RBI totals. We will continue to evaluate the weather reports for **Jorge Polanco** to ensure we don't bleed plate appearances in a rain-shortened affair.",
